# Hero Slider Customization

The homepage hero slider is now a **single-image banner slider**. Do not reintroduce the previous headline + main visual + two action-card slot composition.

## Figma Contract

- Design reference node: `1:2977`
- **Desktop** banner: `1360px × 581px`, aspect `1360 / 581`, radius `34px` (`lg+`)
- **Mobile** banner: `361px × 387px`, aspect `361 / 387`, radius `18px` (`<lg`)
- Storefront rendering must reserve the correct aspect ratio per breakpoint to avoid layout shift.
- Each device image is a complete composed banner. The app does not rebuild Figma text/image layers.

## Data Model

`homeHeroSliderDraft` and `homeHeroSliderPublished` remain JSON fields on settings, but payloads normalize to `version: 3`.

Each slide exposes:

- `imageUrl` / `imageAlt` — desktop banner (required for slide visibility)
- `mobileImageUrl` / `mobileImageAlt` — optional mobile-only banner (falls back to desktop when empty)
- optional `link`
- `order`
- `isActive`
- `autoplayEligible`
- `schedule`
- slide-level `tracking`

Obsolete v2 controls such as foreground/background split images, headline slots, card slots, image overflow, inner borders, typography packages, and device-specific slot trees must not be visible in the admin UI.

## Compatibility

Existing v2 payloads are read safely by the frontend and backend normalizers:

1. Desktop `imageUrl`: prefer `devices.desktop.slots.rightBanner.foregroundImageUrl`, then background, then tablet `heroBanner`.
2. Mobile `mobileImageUrl`: prefer `devices.mobile.slots.heroBanner` foreground/background.
3. Preserve slide id, order, active state, autoplay eligibility, schedule, tracking, alt text, and main-visual link when available.
4. Storefront mobile uses `resolveHeroSlideMobileImage()` (`mobileImageUrl` → fallback `imageUrl`).

No SQL migration is required because the settings fields are JSON.

## Key Files

- [apps/frontend/src/types/super-admin/heroSliderV3.ts](apps/frontend/src/types/super-admin/heroSliderV3.ts) — frontend v3 types and legacy normalization.
- [apps/backend/src/api/settings/services/hero-slider-types.ts](apps/backend/src/api/settings/services/hero-slider-types.ts) — backend v3 types.
- [apps/backend/src/api/settings/services/hero-slider-sanitizers.ts](apps/backend/src/api/settings/services/hero-slider-sanitizers.ts) — backend sanitizer and v2 compatibility.
- [apps/frontend/src/components/Hero/HeroBannerSlider.tsx](apps/frontend/src/components/Hero/HeroBannerSlider.tsx) — storefront slider.
- [apps/frontend/src/components/Hero/config/fromCms.ts](apps/frontend/src/components/Hero/config/fromCms.ts) — CMS to banner slide mapping.
- [apps/frontend/src/components/SuperAdmin/HeroSliderEditor/TemplatePreview.tsx](apps/frontend/src/components/SuperAdmin/HeroSliderEditor/TemplatePreview.tsx) — admin preview and image/link editor.
- [apps/frontend/src/components/SuperAdmin/HeroSliderEditor/SchedulePanel.tsx](apps/frontend/src/components/SuperAdmin/HeroSliderEditor/SchedulePanel.tsx) — slide-level timing/status/tracking.
- [apps/frontend/src/hooks/useHeroSliderEditor.ts](apps/frontend/src/hooks/useHeroSliderEditor.ts) — v3 editor state and slide CRUD.

## Storefront Behavior

- Use the existing optimized image path (`BannerImage` + `imageLoader`).
- Desktop (`lg+`): `width={1360}` `height={581}`, `sizes="(max-width: 1360px) 100vw, 1360px"`, `rounded-[34px]`.
- Mobile (`<lg`): `width={361}` `height={387}`, `sizes="100vw"`, `rounded-[18px]`, separate `mobileImageUrl` when set.
- The first visible slide should be priority-loaded; later slides can lazy-load.
- Keep autoplay, arrows/dots, slide ordering, active status, schedule filtering, and links.

## Admin Editor

- [TemplatePreview.tsx](apps/frontend/src/components/SuperAdmin/HeroSliderEditor/TemplatePreview.tsx) shows desktop + mobile previews and separate upload fields.
- Mobile image upload auto-saves draft (same as desktop upload).
