# Hero Slider Customization

**Description**: This rule documents the hero slider customization system in the super-admin panel. Use it when modifying the hero editor, adding new slots, or configuring fonts.

## Slot Structure

### Desktop
- `topLeftTextBanner` — Headline (title, subtitle, typography)
- `rightBanner` — Main visual (background + foreground image; 1:1 aspect ratio recommended)
- `bottomActionBannerLeft` — Card 1 (image, title, button; product/category image)
- `bottomActionBannerRight` — Card 2 (image, title, button; product/category image)

### Tablet
- `primaryBanner` — Headline
- `heroBanner` — Main visual
- `bottomActionBannerLeft` — Card 1
- `bottomActionBannerRight` — Card 2

### Mobile
- Same slot keys as tablet

## Auto-Sync: Desktop to Tablet and Mobile

When desktop slides are done, tablet and mobile slides can be synced from desktop content:

1. **Manual sync button**: "همگام‌سازی تبلت و موبایل از دسکتاپ" in the PublishBar runs the sync immediately (in-memory, without saving).
2. **Re-save draft**: Backend sanitizers apply updated left-aligned image position defaults for new/empty slots.

**What sync copies from desktop:**
- Content: title, subtitle, images, links, tracking
- Colors: headline/card background colors, title/subtitle/button text colors
- Image positions: card `imageObjectPosition`, main visual `foregroundObjectPosition`

**What sync keeps device-specific (not copied from desktop):**
- Layout: font sizes, class names, image scale/transform classes, content alignment, padding

**Slot mapping** (desktop → tablet/mobile):
| Desktop | Tablet | Mobile |
|---------|--------|--------|
| `topLeftTextBanner` | `primaryBanner` | `primaryBanner` |
| `rightBanner` | `heroBanner` | `heroBanner` |
| `bottomActionBannerLeft` | `bottomActionBannerLeft` | `bottomActionBannerLeft` |
| `bottomActionBannerRight` | `bottomActionBannerRight` | `bottomActionBannerRight` |

**Implementation**: `syncTabletAndMobileFromDesktop` in [apps/frontend/src/types/super-admin/heroSlider.ts](apps/frontend/src/types/super-admin/heroSlider.ts) extracts content and colors from desktop slots, copies image positions, and passes values through `normalizeHeadlineSlot`, `normalizeCardSlot`, `normalizeMainVisualSlot` with device-specific layout defaults.

**Image positioning defaults**: Card images default to `left bottom` on tablet/mobile compact cards; main visual foreground defaults to `bottom center`. Avoid `scale-*` transforms on tablet/mobile — images use `object-contain` inside clipped containers.

## Tablet / Mobile Compact Cards

Storefront and super-admin preview render category cards in **compact** mode on tablet and mobile (`ActionBanner variant="compact"` from `mobileHero.tsx` / `tabletHero.tsx`).

**Layout ratios (approximate, not fixed px):**
- Column gap: `gap-2` (8px scale)
- Headline: `rounded-3xl`
- Main visual: `aspect-[361/245]`, `rounded-[20px]`, foreground contained inside card
- Bottom cards: two columns, `aspect-[176/118]`, `rounded-[20px]`, `overflow-hidden`

**Compact card behavior:**
- Card **title is the only CTA** (arrow + title in one link row); separate subtitle/button stack is hidden
- Link href comes from `buttonHref` / `button.href` / `image.href`
- Background panel sits lower in the card (`top: 22%`, height ~78%) with `rounded-[20px]`
- Product image anchored left-bottom, scaled to fit (~52% card width)
- Default CTA typography: `text-lg font-normal text-neutral-800` (`DEFAULT_COMPACT_CARD_BUTTON_CLASSNAME`)

**Defaults** live in [apps/frontend/src/types/super-admin/heroSlider.ts](apps/frontend/src/types/super-admin/heroSlider.ts) and [apps/backend/src/api/settings/services/hero-slider-default-styles.ts](apps/backend/src/api/settings/services/hero-slider-default-styles.ts). Re-save draft or run desktop→tablet/mobile sync after default changes; existing CMS payloads may retain old `scale-*` class names until re-normalized.

**Editor parity:** [MobileCanvas.tsx](apps/frontend/src/components/SuperAdmin/HeroSliderEditor/canvases/MobileCanvas.tsx) and [TabletCanvas.tsx](apps/frontend/src/components/SuperAdmin/HeroSliderEditor/canvases/TabletCanvas.tsx) mirror the same aspect ratios and `variant="compact"` as storefront.

## CMS Mapping

- Editor payload (`HeroSliderPayload`) is stored via `/settings/hero-slider/draft` (PUT) and published via `/settings/hero-slider/publish` (POST).
- `mapHeroSlideToLayoutsForEditor` in [apps/apps/frontend/src/components/Hero/config/fromCms.ts](apps/apps/frontend/src/components/Hero/config/fromCms.ts) maps `HeroSlideConfig` to `CmsHeroEditorLayouts` (desktop, tablet, mobile).
- Layout specs are applied to Hero components: `TextBanner`, `ActionBanner`, `LeftBanner`.

## Placeholders

When image URLs are empty, the editor uses slot-specific placeholders:
- **Main visual** (`rightBanner` / `heroBanner`): `hero-main-placeholder.svg` — "تصویر اصلی - نسبت ۱:۱ توصیه می‌شود"
- **Cards** (`bottomActionBannerLeft` / `bottomActionBannerRight`): `hero-card-placeholder.svg` — "کارت - تصویر محصول یا دسته‌بندی"

Files: [apps/apps/frontend/public/images/placeholders/](apps/apps/frontend/public/images/placeholders/)

## Font Configuration

To add new fonts for the hero font selector:

1. Add font files under `packages/fonts/assets/` (keep woff2 paths consistent).
2. Register with `next/font/local` in [`packages/fonts/src/index.ts`](packages/fonts/src/index.ts) and export the loader; consume from `@repo/fonts` in `apps/frontend/src/app/layout.tsx` (html `variable` classes).
3. Add the font to Tailwind in `apps/frontend/tailwind.config.ts` under `fontFamily`
4. Add the option to `HERO_FONT_FAMILY_OPTIONS` in [apps/apps/frontend/src/types/super-admin/heroSlider.ts](apps/apps/frontend/src/types/super-admin/heroSlider.ts)

## Background Image URLs

Strapi stores image paths like `/uploads/...`. At **render time**, `LeftBanner` and `ActionBanner` resolve these to absolute URLs using [apps/apps/frontend/src/utils/resolveAssetUrl.ts](apps/apps/frontend/src/utils/resolveAssetUrl.ts) (and `NEXT_PUBLIC_IMAGE_BASE_URL`) so background images load correctly. Stored payloads remain path-only; resolution is not persisted.

## Hero Editor File Layout

- **TemplatePreview.tsx** — Main preview + device switcher + side panel; imports from editors, canvases, utils.
- **utils.ts** — `getFrameByDevice`, `slotLabelMap`, `makeLayoutsSafe`, `resolveColorForInput`, `safeImageSrc`; exports `DeviceMode`, `SlotKey`.
- **EditableSlot.tsx** — Wrapper for click-to-edit slots in the preview.
- **editors/** — Slot editors: `TextStyleEditor`, `HeadlineEditor`, `MainVisualEditor`, `CardEditor`, `SlotEditorContent` (index re-exports).
- **canvases/** — Device-specific preview canvases: `DesktopCanvas`, `TabletCanvas`, `MobileCanvas`.

## Style Packages (Presets)

Headline and card slots support **پکیج استایل** (Apply preset). Presets are defined in [apps/apps/frontend/src/types/super-admin/heroSliderPackages.ts](apps/apps/frontend/src/types/super-admin/heroSliderPackages.ts): `HERO_HEADLINE_STYLE_PRESETS` and `HERO_CARD_STYLE_PRESETS` (e.g. مینیمال, بولد, الگنت). Selecting a preset merges its `titleStyle` / `subtitleStyle` or `titleStyle` / `buttonStyle` into the current slot.

## Font Size Labels (xl, 2xl, 3xl)

Font size is controlled via a **px range slider** (12–96px) in `TextStyleEditor`. Values are stored as Tailwind arbitrary tokens (`text-[32px]`) internally — admins never see raw class names in the UI.

Legacy preset tokens from style packages remain valid; the slider reads them via `fontSizeTokenToPx()` and writes `pxToFontSizeToken()` on change.

**Rendering:** px slider values (`text-[Npx]`) are applied as inline `fontSize` in `TextBanner` / `ActionBanner` because Tailwind only emits CSS for classes present at build time — not for arbitrary runtime px values.

Helpers: `fontSizeTokenToPx`, `pxToFontSizeToken`, `resolveFontSizeToken`, `fontSizeTokenToInlineStyle` in [heroSlider.ts](apps/frontend/src/types/super-admin/heroSlider.ts).

## Background & image scale sliders

- **Main visual / card background scale**: 50–200% slider → `backgroundSize` (`cover` at 100%, else `${n}% auto`)
- **Card product image width**: 20–100% → `imageCustomWidth`
- **Card product image position**: preset + horizontal/vertical **−50% to 150%** → `imageObjectPosition` (anchor layout in `ActionBanner`)
- **Main visual foreground width**: 20–100% → `foregroundCustomWidth`
- **Foreground zoom**: 0.5–2 (unchanged)
- **Headline title–subtitle gap**: 0–64px → `titleSubtitleGapPx` (inline flex `gap` on `TextBanner`)
- **Headline block bottom margin**: 0–160px slider → `bottomMarginPx`
- **Main visual foreground position**: preset + horizontal/vertical **−100% to 200%** anchor sliders
- **Main visual foreground nudge**: **±600px** offset sliders
- **Main visual foreground width**: **10–250%**
- **Main visual foreground height**: **20–200%** (100% = auto)
- **Foreground zoom**: **0.25×–3×**

Helpers: `objectPositionToPercents`, `percentsToObjectPosition`, `objectPositionPresetValue` in [heroSlider.ts](apps/frontend/src/types/super-admin/heroSlider.ts).

Shared UI: [SizeRangeControl.tsx](apps/frontend/src/components/SuperAdmin/HeroSliderEditor/editors/SizeRangeControl.tsx)

## Inner border (کادر داخلی)

Main visual and card slots support an inset decorative border (`innerBorder`: enabled, color, width 0–12px, offset 0–48px).

- Edited in **کادر داخلی** sections of [MainVisualEditor.tsx](apps/frontend/src/components/SuperAdmin/HeroSliderEditor/editors/MainVisualEditor.tsx) and [CardEditor.tsx](apps/frontend/src/components/SuperAdmin/HeroSliderEditor/editors/CardEditor.tsx).
- Rendered **inside the background panel, under the foreground/product image** (color backgrounds only).
- Persisted through the backend sanitizer in [hero-slider-sanitizers.ts](apps/backend/src/api/settings/services/hero-slider-sanitizers.ts) (`sanitizeHeroInnerBorder`).
- Desktop inner borders sync to tablet/mobile on desktop→device sync ([heroSlider.ts](apps/frontend/src/types/super-admin/heroSlider.ts)).

